# Example 11: a reaction coordinate as an ordered color ramp.
# The five states of multi-turnover SpCas9 from Kiernan et al. 2025,
# Nat Commun 16:5681 (Taylor lab): pre-activation, precleavage,
# checkpoint, product, dissociated.
#
# Rule: when panels are steps in a process, do not give them categorical
# colors. Use one ordered ramp, assign it in process order, and reuse the
# same ramp everywhere else the states appear: the progression arrow, a
# bar of class occupancy, the map thumbnails. The reader learns it once.
#
# The ramp here is teal to orange, monotonic in lightness so it survives
# grayscale printing. Defined as lab_state1..5 in palettes/lab_colors.cxc.
open 9eak
open 9eal
open 9ed9
open 9eda
open 9edb
open ../../palettes/lab_colors.cxc
open ../../presets/Base/publication_white.cxc

# Superpose every state on the first
matchmaker #2/A to #1/A
matchmaker #3/A to #1/A
matchmaker #4/A to #1/A
matchmaker #5/A to #1/A

# One ramp step per state, protein only. Nucleic acids stay neutral so the
# ramp reads as the process coordinate and not as a chain identity.
color #1/A lab_state1
color #2/A lab_state2
color #3/A lab_state3
color #4/A lab_state4
color #5/A lab_state5
color nucleic lab_gray_p

view #1/A
turn y 30
view #1/A pad 0.08

hide #2,3,4,5 models
2dlabels text "I  pre-activation" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.94 size 22 color lab_state1 bold true
save state1.png width 2800 supersample 3

hide #1 models
show #2 models
2dlabels delete all
2dlabels text "II  precleavage" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.94 size 22 color lab_state2 bold true
save state2.png width 2800 supersample 3

hide #2 models
show #3 models
2dlabels delete all
2dlabels text "III  checkpoint" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.94 size 22 color lab_state3 bold true
save state3.png width 2800 supersample 3

hide #3 models
show #4 models
2dlabels delete all
2dlabels text "IV  product" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.94 size 22 color lab_state4 bold true
save state4.png width 2800 supersample 3

hide #4 models
show #5 models
2dlabels delete all
2dlabels text "V  dissociated" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.94 size 22 color lab_state5 bold true
save state5.png width 2800 supersample 3

# The ramp as its own legend strip, to sit under the row of panels or
# inside the progression arrow in the final layout.
hide #5 models
2dlabels delete all
key lab_state1:I lab_state2:II lab_state3:III lab_state4:IV lab_state5:V pos 0.08,0.42 size 0.84,0.16 fontSize 30 colorTreatment distinct labelSide right/bottom
save ramp_legend.png width 2800 supersample 3
